{% comment %}
  Fixes single-cover product-page sizing to a consistent height with natural
  (per-cover) width, left-aligned on the page's left rail, plus a light book-cover shadow and a crisp
  charcoal outline. Overrides Horizon's forced aspect-ratio: 1/1.25 and
  constrain-height cap (and its grid/flex stretch), which otherwise render
  portrait covers small/centred with empty space, or too tall.

  Everything is scoped to .product-information__media and gated on :only-child,
  so multi-image galleries (multiple sibling .product-media-container elements)
  keep native Horizon behaviour untouched. No !important — specificity alone
  (.product-information__media .product-media-container:only-child img = 0,3,1)
  beats base.css and the media-fit-cover rule.

  ALIGNMENT HISTORY — read before changing how the cover sits:
    8 Jul 2026  — flush left, inset by --gz-gutter (24px) to match the Synopsis
                  band's inner gutter.
    18 Aug 2026 — centred in its column, to suit a bounded 400px media column.
    18 Aug 2026 — REVERTED, same day: flush left again, and now with NO gutter
                  inset. The page is aligned to ONE pair of vertical rails, and
                  the left rail is the media column's own left edge. A centred
                  cover cannot define a rail: cover width is natural per title,
                  so a centred left edge lands at a different x for every book.
                  The 24px inset is gone because the band no longer carries
                  inline padding either — both sections are flush at the rail.

  18 Aug 2026, later — HERO OPTS OUT OF THE SHARED SPLIT. It briefly used
  --gz-grid-columns / --gz-grid-gap alongside the band; it now uses its own tight
  left-aligned pair (460px panel + 48px + max 520px buy box = 1028px) that stops
  short of the right rail on purpose, per the Fitzcarraldo reference. The BAND
  still uses those tokens and still spans rail to rail. Left rail is shared; the
  right rail is a band-only edge.

  The cover also now sits inside a fixed 460x560 tinted PANEL rather than being
  sized directly — same silhouette on every product page whatever the cover's
  aspect ratio.

  Render on the product template, e.g. {% render 'gazelle-cover-styles' %}.
{% endcomment %}

{% style %}
  /* Page width (1200px) is now set globally in snippets/gazelle-layout.liquid —
     the local --page-width override that used to live here has been removed. */

  /* THE COVER PANEL. A fixed 460x560 tinted panel, flush to the left rail, with
     the cover image centred on both axes inside it. Fixed size regardless of the
     cover's aspect ratio — that is the point: every product page presents the
     same silhouette, and tall/short/wide covers no longer change the layout.
     The container is already `display: flex` from base.css, so centring is just
     align-items / justify-content. */
  .product-information__media .product-media-container:only-child {
    aspect-ratio: auto;                 /* kill the forced 1/1.25 */
    width: 460px;
    height: 560px;
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: none;                   /* overrides Horizon's constrain-height cap */
    background: #f3efe8;                /* paper, one step darker than --gz-paper #faf7f2 */
    border-radius: 2px;
    margin-inline: 0;                   /* flush to the media column's left edge = the page's left rail */
    margin-block-start: 24px;           /* align panel top with title (details block padding-block-start: 24) */
    align-self: start;                  /* stop stretching to fill the cell */
    justify-self: start;                /* flush left — see ALIGNMENT HISTORY */
    align-items: center;                /* centre the cover vertically in the panel */
    justify-content: center;            /* centre the cover horizontally in the panel */
    overflow: visible;                  /* so the image's shadow isn't clipped */
  }

  /* Centre the cover inside the panel. .constrain-height is required so
     specificity (0,4,0) beats the theme's
     .product-media-container.constrain-height:has(...) rule (0,3,0), which
     would otherwise re-assert its own justify-content. */
  .product-information__media .product-media-container.constrain-height:only-child {
    justify-content: center;
  }

  /* .product-media is `display: flex; flex: 1` in base.css:1902, so it would
     stretch across the whole panel and the image would sit left, not centred.
     Shrink it to its content and centre within it. */
  .product-information__media .product-media-container:only-child .product-media {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .product-information__media .product-media-container:only-child img {
    aspect-ratio: auto;
    object-fit: contain;                /* never crop a cover; beats media-fit-cover */
    height: auto;
    max-height: 480px;                  /* 40px of panel breathing room top and bottom */
    width: auto;                        /* natural width per cover, no distortion */
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  /* Border + shadow on the actual cover image. Explicit .product-media__image
     (0,4,0) is unambiguous and beats the theme's .product-media > * rule. */
  .product-information__media .product-media-container:only-child .product-media__image {
    border: 1px solid #1a1917;          /* crisp charcoal outline */
    border-radius: 2px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(26, 25, 23, 0.1);
  }

  /* Stop the theme's overflow:hidden on the media wrappers (>=750px) from
     clipping the soft shadow. */
  .product-information__media .product-media-container:only-child .product-media,
  .product-information__media .product-media-container:only-child .product-media > * {
    overflow: visible;
  }

  /* Hero columns — a TIGHT LEFT-ALIGNED PAIR, deliberately NOT the shared split.
     460px panel + 48px gap + a buy box capped at 520px = 1028px, sitting inside
     the 1200px rails and stopping 172px short of the right rail on purpose
     (Fitzcarraldo reference). `justify-content: start` pins that leftover space
     to the right instead of distributing it between the tracks.

     The band still uses --gz-grid-columns / --gz-grid-gap and still spans rail
     to rail; only the hero opts out.

     Specificity (0,4,0) beats the native (0,3,0) rules at
     product-information-content.liquid:169 and :288.

     Note the column-gap: Horizon does NOT put a gap on this grid. The section
     sets `gap: var(--gap) 0` (row 48, column ZERO) and fakes the gutter with
     padding-right / padding-left of --gap/2 on the two columns. That padding is
     zeroed below so the gutter comes from a real column-gap instead — otherwise
     the panel sits 24px inside the left rail. */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .product-information .product-information__grid.product-information--media-left:not(.product-information--media-none) {
      grid-template-columns: 460px minmax(0, 520px);
      column-gap: 48px;
      justify-content: start;
    }

    /* Zero core's half-gutter padding. Core declares it at 0,4,0
       (.product-information__grid:not(...).product-information--media-left
        .product-information__media), so these need 0,5,0 to win outright rather
       than depending on stylesheet source order. */
    .product-information .product-information__grid.product-information--media-left:not(.product-information--media-none) .product-information__media {
      padding-right: 0;
    }

    .product-information .product-information__grid.product-information--media-left:not(.product-information--media-none) .product-details {
      padding-left: 0;
    }
  }

  /* Below 750px the columns stack, so the fixed panel becomes fluid: full column
     width at a 4/5 aspect instead of 460x560. The image cap drops to 100% of the
     panel — a flat 480px would overflow a panel that is only ~420px tall on a
     375px-wide phone. */
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .product-information__media .product-media-container:only-child {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    }

    .product-information__media .product-media-container:only-child img {
      max-height: 100%;
    }
  }

  /* Sticky cover — HEADER OFFSET ONLY. The sticky itself is native.
     <media-gallery> already carries Horizon's `sticky-content` class,
     unconditionally and with no setting gating it
     (snippets/product-media-gallery-content.liquid:338), and base.css:2574
     gives that class `position: sticky; top: var(--sticky-header-offset, 0)`.
     media-gallery is `display: block` with no height (base.css:1589) inside a
     stretched grid item, so it has travel. We therefore add NO position and NO
     top of our own — that would be re-implementing native behaviour.

     The one real gap: core assigns --sticky-header-offset to the BUY BOX only
     (product-information-content.liquid:314, scoped to
     `.product-details.sticky-content--desktop`). The media column is left on the
     `0` fallback, so with the header set to enable_sticky_header: "always" the
     cover sticks flush to the viewport top and slides UNDER the header on scroll.
     Victim: anyone scrolling a product page — the cover is progressively hidden
     behind the header exactly when the sticky is meant to keep it visible.

     Fix reuses core's own condition and token, retargeted at the gallery.
     Deliberately NOT :only-child gated, unlike the sizing rules above: a
     multi-image gallery slides under the header just the same, and this
     corrects a native offset rather than restyling the gallery.
     Desktop only — below 750px the columns stack and sticky travel is unwanted. */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    body:has(#header-group #header-component[data-sticky-state='active'])
      .product-information__media media-gallery {
      --sticky-header-offset: var(--header-height);
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}
